# Everything the image does not need, and two things it must not have.
#
# `.env` holds the API keys and `.data` holds real documents and the signing
# key. Both would otherwise be copied into the image and travel with it
# wherever it is pushed.
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
# And the frontend's, which sets VITE_API_URL to a development machine. Baked
# into a build it makes the deployed page call 127.0.0.1 — the reader's own
# computer — and fail as though the server were down.
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.*
!frontend/.env.example
backend/.data/
**/secret.key

.git/
.gitignore
.claude/

backend/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
backend/tests/

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
README.md
